## Structure (Event-Driven / Event Sourcing)

```
src/
├── features/<module>/           ← per-feature slice
│   ├── commands/                 ← command + handler (write path)
│   ├── events/                   ← domain event classes
│   ├── aggregates/               ← event-sourced aggregate
│   ├── projections/              ← read model builder
│   ├── event-store/              ← append-only event log
│   ├── dto/                      ← HTTP request shapes
│   └── infrastructure/           ← controller, module, outbox
```

**Write path:** Controller → Command → Handler → Aggregate → Event Store → Outbox → Broker
**Read path:**  Controller → Projection (denormalized read model)

Domain events are the single source of truth. Every state change is an immutable event appended
to the event store. Aggregates rebuild their state by replaying events. Projections subscribe
to events and maintain fast, denormalized read models.

The outbox pattern guarantees that events are reliably published to Kafka/RabbitMQ even if
the broker is temporarily unavailable — events are written to the outbox table atomically
with the event store and published asynchronously.

